WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.342 --> 00:00:01.780
- I feel like Man Versus Food right now,

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:04.294
this is the point where like, it hits you.

00:00:04.294 --> 00:00:06.640
And you feel like you're gonna die.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.973
- Eat, eat, eat!

00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:10.680
(laughing)

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.842
(squeaking of dry erase marker)

00:00:12.842 --> 00:00:14.288
(turkey gobbling)

00:00:14.288 --> 00:00:16.533
- I have never been in a
food competition before.

00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:19.477
- I have never participated
in any food eating

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:21.159
competition before.

00:00:21.159 --> 00:00:25.255
- In fifth grade I was
third in a Twinkie eating

00:00:25.255 --> 00:00:27.349
contest at my elementary school.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:29.636
I've done the Buffalo Wild
Wings hot wing challenge,

00:00:29.636 --> 00:00:33.251
I've eaten the monster
burrito at Freebird's.

00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:35.465
That's technically a competition.

00:00:35.465 --> 00:00:37.190
Y'all are gonna see me
throw up or pass out.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:38.794
Either way, it's not
gonna end well for me.

00:00:38.794 --> 00:00:40.296
- There are three of us.

00:00:40.296 --> 00:00:42.708
- Three versus one, like
there has to be some sort

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.957
of odds in our favor.

00:00:44.957 --> 00:00:45.994
- Hi, I'm Yasir Salem.

00:00:45.994 --> 00:00:47.188
I'm a competitive eater, a marathon eater,

00:00:47.188 --> 00:00:48.744
and a triathelete.

00:00:48.744 --> 00:00:51.394
I took the world record
in corn on the cob in 2016

00:00:51.394 --> 00:00:53.950
with 47 corn on the cob in 12 minutes.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.495
I've also set the record for cannoli,

00:00:56.495 --> 00:00:59.024
I believe it was 30
somewhat in six minutes.

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:02.591
And I also hold multiple
records in the Tour du Donut

00:01:02.591 --> 00:01:06.314
bicycle races, and my
record there is 61 donuts

00:01:06.314 --> 00:01:07.981
over a 29 mile race.

00:01:09.409 --> 00:01:12.397
The challenge here for the other team is,

00:01:12.397 --> 00:01:14.499
they're gonna have to move
pretty quickly through

00:01:14.499 --> 00:01:15.807
the food.

00:01:15.807 --> 00:01:17.402
It might not be a ton
of food for each person,

00:01:17.402 --> 00:01:20.835
but I can take down that
amount of food much quicker

00:01:20.835 --> 00:01:22.011
than they can.

00:01:22.011 --> 00:01:25.094
(driving rock music)

00:01:33.262 --> 00:01:34.267
- Yes!
- Yeah!

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:35.276
- This is so much food!

00:01:35.276 --> 00:01:37.526
(cheering)

00:01:42.774 --> 00:01:45.843
- [Referee] Three, two, one, thanksgiving!

00:01:45.843 --> 00:01:48.343
(silly music)

00:01:51.171 --> 00:01:52.599
- Can't breathe!

00:01:52.599 --> 00:01:54.055
- [Kayla] Need bigger bites!

00:01:54.055 --> 00:01:55.784
- This is good!

00:01:55.784 --> 00:01:57.869
- Oh my god, you guys.

00:01:57.869 --> 00:01:59.567
This is so hard!

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.186
- This is gonna ruin Thanksgiving for me.

00:02:01.186 --> 00:02:02.838
- Everytime I swallow
I think I'm gonna die.

00:02:02.838 --> 00:02:05.130
(groaning)

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.328
- [Kayla] He finished that whole things.

00:02:07.328 --> 00:02:09.578
(mumbling)

00:02:12.562 --> 00:02:13.970
(belching)

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.256
(crowd groaning)

00:02:15.256 --> 00:02:17.223
- He's pushing into a ball!

00:02:17.223 --> 00:02:18.511
- My jaw!

00:02:18.511 --> 00:02:19.814
How is he doing this?

00:02:19.814 --> 00:02:21.484
- Yo, we can beat him!

00:02:21.484 --> 00:02:23.158
We can actually beat him!

00:02:23.158 --> 00:02:24.782
Come on!

00:02:24.782 --> 00:02:26.422
- I like already feel nauseous.

00:02:26.422 --> 00:02:27.488
(mumbling)

00:02:27.488 --> 00:02:29.321
Eric, flash him!

00:02:29.321 --> 00:02:31.479
- Look at my boobs!

00:02:31.479 --> 00:02:33.170
- Focus, dammit!

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.086
- Why is there more food,
it feels like it keeps

00:02:35.086 --> 00:02:36.323
appearing!

00:02:36.323 --> 00:02:37.683
- I could possibly throw up.

00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:40.385
I'm not going to, but in
the future may throw up.

00:02:40.385 --> 00:02:43.302
(triumphant music)

00:02:46.526 --> 00:02:48.589
- He's laughing, he's making him laugh!

00:02:48.589 --> 00:02:50.264
- I guess I'll wash it down with gravy.

00:02:50.264 --> 00:02:51.944
(groaning)

00:02:51.944 --> 00:02:53.494
Whoa, we're almost done!

00:02:53.494 --> 00:02:56.403
Medically I feel like I
should not eat anymore food.

00:02:56.403 --> 00:02:58.273
I don't need to.

00:02:58.273 --> 00:03:00.916
I've eaten turkey, gravy, mashed potatoes,

00:03:00.916 --> 00:03:04.584
corn, stuffing, pie,
in like three minutes.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.474
I don't wanna!

00:03:06.474 --> 00:03:08.049
- You can do it!

00:03:08.049 --> 00:03:08.882
- I know!

00:03:10.002 --> 00:03:11.042
- Are you tapping out?

00:03:11.042 --> 00:03:12.082
- We're not tapping out.

00:03:12.082 --> 00:03:13.124
- Okay.

00:03:13.124 --> 00:03:16.355
- We're discussing, but
we haven't tapped out yet.

00:03:16.355 --> 00:03:17.900
There's not much more room here.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.801
The medical professional, should I stop?

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:21.227
- Feel like passing out?

00:03:21.227 --> 00:03:22.924
- I feel like I'm either
gonna shit my pants

00:03:22.924 --> 00:03:24.297
or I'm gonna throw up.

00:03:24.297 --> 00:03:25.919
I've proven enough to myself.

00:03:25.919 --> 00:03:27.728
I'm tapping out.

00:03:27.728 --> 00:03:28.734
- Good job, team!

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:31.408
- I don't know what we
proved or what we did,

00:03:31.408 --> 00:03:33.404
but we got (mumbling)!

00:03:33.404 --> 00:03:35.524
To do things, with our mouths.

00:03:35.524 --> 00:03:37.672
(laughing)

00:03:37.672 --> 00:03:39.549
Y'all are gonna see me
throw up or pass out,

00:03:39.549 --> 00:03:41.132
either way it's not gonna end well for me.

00:03:41.132 --> 00:03:41.965
(gagging)

00:03:41.965 --> 00:03:43.410
(chiming)

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.617
- The other team did a
lot better than I thought,

00:03:45.617 --> 00:03:48.905
but they tapped out and I
encourage them next time,

00:03:48.905 --> 00:03:49.908
let's do this again.

00:03:49.908 --> 00:03:51.963
- I honestly wasn't
very confident going in,

00:03:51.963 --> 00:03:53.845
and as soon as I put
that turkey in my mouth,

00:03:53.845 --> 00:03:56.917
that first bite, I knew
was not gonna go well.

00:03:56.917 --> 00:03:59.141
- Food for five people,
three people, it's like,

00:03:59.141 --> 00:04:00.444
surely we can do that.

00:04:00.444 --> 00:04:01.820
And then I saw the food,
and I was like, nope.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.286
- All things aside, it's
always cool to see how

00:04:03.286 --> 00:04:05.844
far the human body can go.

00:04:05.844 --> 00:04:07.417
I feel like we tested our limits today.

00:04:07.417 --> 00:04:08.422
- Yeah.

00:04:08.422 --> 00:04:09.589
- We didn't hold back.

00:04:09.589 --> 00:04:10.850
We bonded.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:11.855
- Good team bonding.

00:04:11.855 --> 00:04:14.096
- Now it'll just make me
appreciate Thanksgiving

00:04:14.096 --> 00:04:15.761
that much more knowing
I don't have to eat it

00:04:15.761 --> 00:04:19.025
in three minutes with three
pounds of food and gravy.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:22.525
(upbeat electronic music)

00:04:29.477 --> 00:04:32.047
(squeaking of dry erase markers)

